{
 "section_summary": "The section opens with the continuation of a report on Japanese civilian intelligence organizations, including the Greater East Asia Ministry, the Shanghai consulate, and the East Asia Tung Wen Academy. It then contains a family's appeal for Hajimu Masuda's return from Shanghai, reports on Japanese fishermen detained in Chinese waters, and 1949 telegrams about Chinese contacts seeking trade with Japan. Several scans contain only a document header or little legible text.",
